// Counter invariants of the Expr core (include/sea/Expr/ExprCore.hh,
// fatalCounter): always checked (Release too), fail at the cause, no
// recovery. unittests/ExprCore: the last allowed count and id, ordinary
// release, duplicate terms, id reset on recycling, lookup before
// building (no operator clone, no id on a hit), the watch of node
// creation (every step nodes made, not on a hit), scoped marks (nested
// scopes, clear and reuse, recycled nodes unmarked, the two-bit use count);
// then each broken invariant aborts before the counter changes, and a
// mark scope beyond the 64 bits or given a node of another factory aborts
// (no fallback), naming the live leases.
RUN: sea-expr-core-test | FileCheck %s
CHECK: test: limits ok
CHECK: test: lifecycle ok
CHECK: test: reclamation ok
CHECK: test: lookup ok
CHECK: test: watch ok
CHECK: test: marks ok
CHECK: failures: 0
RUN: not --crash sea-expr-core-test refcount-overflow 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OVF
OVF: error: [expr.refcount-overflow] Expr counter invariant broken: {{.*}} value=4294967295
OVF-NOT: no crash
RUN: not --crash sea-expr-core-test refcount-underflow 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=UNF
UNF: error: [expr.refcount-underflow] Expr counter invariant broken: {{.*}} value=0
UNF-NOT: no crash
RUN: not --crash sea-expr-core-test id-exhausted 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=IDX
IDX: error: [expr.id-exhausted] Expr counter invariant broken: {{.*}} value=4294967295
IDX-NOT: no crash
RUN: not --crash sea-expr-core-test marks-exhausted 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MEX
MEX: error: [expr.marks-exhausted] no free Expr mark bit: scope 'use-count' needs 2, {{.*}} has 63 live leases
MEX: lease: bit=0 owner=leaked-walk
MEX: lease: bit=62 owner=leaked-walk
MEX-NOT: no crash
RUN: not --crash sea-expr-core-test marks-factory 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MFA
MFA: error: [expr.marks-factory] a node of factory {{.*}} given to a mark scope of factory
MFA: lease: bit=0 owner=s
MFA-NOT: no crash

